~ default
It's default

~ opening
Hey... little one. Are you alright??
This isn’t exactly a good place to fall asleep, you know.
- Who are you?
	Elvic: I am Elvic.
	Elvic: Don’t worry… I’m not a bad person.
	Elvic: Just someone passing by. I came to see the statue.
Elvic: But, hey, I don’t think I’ve seen you around before.
Elvic: Where did you come from?

- I don't know
	Elvic: Umm... Did you lose your memory?
	Elvic: Hm. That’s a rather classic story, isn’t it?
	Elvic: ...Sorry. Forget I said that.
	
- I am not from this world
	Elvic: Oh...?
	Elvic: ...That’s an interesting way to put it.
	Elvic: You’ve got quite an imagination.
	Elvic: Well, it’s okay. I’ve heard all kinds of things before.
Elvic: Why don’t you take a walk through the village?
Elvic: It’s just up ahead. You might find something interesting there.
Elvic: Or... you could just go back to sleep here. I wouldn’t mind.
Elvic: I still have something I need to take care of here.
Elvic: See you around.
=> END

~ statue
It’s an angel statue.
One of its wings is broken.
There is something written on it.
"Guarding the truth,
Carry the hope.
To be eternal is to be alone."
=> END

~ sign
It's a wooden signpost.
Northeast\: Village
So--hwes-\: --i--d M----
The words on the lower sign are almost unreadable, as though they were deliberately scratched out
=> END

~ trail_elvic
Elvic: Hey, wait a second!
Elvic: I just realized... you’re new here, right?
Elvic: You must not know your way around yet.
Elvic: Umm, you might need some help getting around.
Elvic: Come with me,
Elvic: I know someone who can tell you more about this village.
=> END

~ self_talk
Elvic: There’s no time left... What should I do...?
Elvic: Was everything I’ve done... really the right choice...?
=> END

